# Negative controls for the listing step (plan 04-15, D-26, D-29): one per token. The positive
# control is the toy cart listing of controls/_good/tree; the bootstub-* controls overlay a toy
# boot stub, its inventory line and a toy-stub profile with the two vector fields.
# Plan 07-04 (A-10): the positive toy listing holds one valid DATA word; listing-data-in-operand-slot and
# listing-data-after-sdbd are the two places a DATA word is refused (operand pending, directly after SDBD).
listing-bits-mismatch
listing-row-mismatch
listing-operand-count
listing-range
listing-header
listing-unlisted
bootstub-size
bootstub-row
bootstub-vector
listing-branch-target-mismatch
listing-branch-target-missing
listing-sdbd-operand-missing
listing-sdbd-carry-over
listing-sdbd-prefix-before-branch
listing-sdbd-target-mvo
listing-sdbd-target-zero
listing-sdbd-indirect-mode
listing-operand-count-after-sdbd
listing-data-in-operand-slot
listing-data-after-sdbd
